<title>GERMANY: No formal G7 communique expected - US spokesman.</title>
<headline>No formal G7 communique expected - US spokesman.</headline>
<dateline>BERLIN 1997-02-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Group of Seven industrialised nations will not issue a formal communique following their economic talks on Saturday, a U.S. Treasury spokesman said.</p>
<p>&quot;There will be no communique. My understanding is that there won't be any common statements,&quot; the spokesman told reporters.</p>
<p>When asked if there would be any written statement at all, the spokesman said no, suggesting that each of the delegations would put forward their own views on the meeting individually.</p>
<p>The U.S. Germany, Japan, France, Italy, Canada and Britain are members of the G7.</p>
<p>--Berlin Newsroom, +49 30 2039810</p>
